    "tpb_seq": 1,
    "tpb_book": "<div><strong>無指定教科書，採用教師課程筆記或自製講義。</strong></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><strong>如需要複習經濟學原理，有以下參考書可供參考(舊版也沒有關係)</strong></div>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Mankiw, N. G. (2023). 經濟學原理 (王銘正譯)。東華。</li>\n\t<li>朱敬一 等人 (2025) 基礎經濟學 (第十版)。華泰。</li>\n\t<li>吳聰敏、樊家忠 (2023) 經濟學原理(第四版)。雙葉書廊。</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<div>Jean Tirole (2025) 邁向共善：諾貝爾經濟學獎得主永續建言，如何實現人類最大多數的幸福！(郁保林譯)。聯經。</div>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
    "tpb_book_en": null
  },
  "readings": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CM03122",
    "sub_id": "04900",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpc_seq": 1,
    "tpc_book": "<div><strong>參考書</strong></div>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Evans, A. W. (2004). <em>Economics, Real Estate and the Supply of Land</em>. Wiley.</li>\n\t<li>Tietenberg, T. and Lewis, L. (2018). <em>Environmental and Natural Resource Economics</em>. Routledge.</li>\n\t<li>Hussen, A. M. (2001). <em>Principle of Environmental Economics: Economics, Ecology, and Public Policy </em>(陳凱俐譯). 揚智。</li>\n\t<li>Sieg, H. (2020). <em>Urban Economics and Fiscal Policy</em>. Princeton University Press.</li>\n\t<li>李春長 (2012)。「不動產經濟學」。臺北：智勝。</li>\n\t<li>林森田、丁秀吟 (2017)。「土地經濟學」 (第二版)。臺北：巨流。</li>\n\t<li>林鐘雄 (2020)。「西洋經濟思想史」 (第七版)。臺北：三民。</li>\n\t<li>殷章甫 (2008)。「土地經濟學」。臺北：五南。</li>\n\t<li>韓乾 (2013)。「土地資源經濟學」。臺北：五南。</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div><strong>期刊文章</strong></div>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Allen, T., &amp; Arkolakis, C. (2023). Economic activity across space: A supply and demand approach.&nbsp;<em>Journal of Economic Perspectives</em>,&nbsp;<em>37</em>(2), 3-28.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.regsciurbeco.2025.104086\" target=\"_blank\">https://doi.org/10.1257/jep.37.2.3</a></li>\n\t<li>Brueckner, J. K. (2025). Work-from-home and cities: An elementary spatial model.&nbsp;<em>Regional Science and Urban Economics</em>, Article 104086.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.regsciurbeco.2025.104086\" target=\"_blank\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.regsciurbeco.2025.104086</a></li>\n\t<li>Garza, N., and Gonzalez, I. (2021). An urban system assessment of land value capture: the Colombian case.&nbsp;<em>Land Use Policy</em>,&nbsp;<em>109</em>, Article 105598.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landusepol.2021.105598\" target=\"_blank\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.landusepol.2021.105598</a></li>\n\t<li>Alterman, R. (2011).&nbsp;Land-Use Regulations and Property Values: The &ldquo;Windfalls Capture&rdquo; Idea Revisited,&nbsp;in N. Brooks, K. Donaghy, and G.‐J.&nbsp;Knaap (eds),&nbsp;<em>The Oxford Handbook of Urban Economics and Planning</em>, Oxford Handbooks.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780195380620.013.0034\">https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780195380620.013.0034</a></li>\n\t<li>Hsu, W. T. (2012). Central place theory and city size distribution.&nbsp;<em>The Economic Journal</em>,&nbsp;<em>122</em>(563), 903-932.&nbsp;<br />\n\t<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1468-0297.2012.02518.x\">https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1468-0297.2012.02518.x</a>&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>Ossokina, I. V., Svitak, J., and Teulings, C. N. (2024). The urban economics of retail.&nbsp;<em>Regional Science and Urban Economics</em>,&nbsp;<em>108</em>, Article 104026.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.regsciurbeco.2024.104026\" target=\"_blank\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.regsciurbeco.2024.104026</a></li>\n</ol>\n",
    "tpc_book_en": null
  },
